1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,920
A year ago, the sign at your gas station said $3.07.

2
00:00:04,920 --> 00:00:09,280
This spring it went past four and a half, and this month, for the first time since July, it dropped

3
00:00:09,280 --> 00:00:10,760
back under 4.

4
00:00:10,760 --> 00:00:12,720
Oil has fallen 3 weeks in a row.

5
00:00:12,720 --> 00:00:15,560
So the war must be ending, right?

6
00:00:15,560 --> 00:00:16,800
Not even close.

7
00:00:16,800 --> 00:00:19,920
Because the price of oil right now is not really about oil.

8
00:00:19,920 --> 00:00:22,560
It is about a war that Congress never voted for.

9
00:00:22,560 --> 00:00:27,520
An election that just flipped Washington upside down and 3 million pages of files with one

10
00:00:27,520 --> 00:00:30,320
name in them that will not go away.

11
00:00:30,320 --> 00:00:34,440
By the end of this you will know why oil is falling, why the next 6 weeks may be the

12
00:00:34,440 --> 00:00:39,360
most dangerous of this whole war, and what the number on that gas sign has to do

13
00:00:39,360 --> 00:00:41,160
with Jeffrey Epstein.

14
00:00:41,160 --> 00:00:42,960
Let's go back to the start of this year.

15
00:00:42,960 --> 00:00:47,720
On the 30th of January the Justice Department released more than 3 million pages of the

16
00:00:47,720 --> 00:00:49,760
Epstein files.

17
00:00:49,760 --> 00:00:52,640
The president's name appears in them many times.

18
00:00:52,640 --> 00:00:56,840
Being named in those files is not proof of a crime and the Justice Department said some

19
00:00:56,840 --> 00:01:00,280
of the claims about him were untrue and sensational.

20
00:01:00,280 --> 00:01:02,560
But the files were the biggest story in America.

21
00:01:02,560 --> 00:01:07,680
A month later, on the 28th of February, the United States and Israel launched strikes

22
00:01:07,680 --> 00:01:08,680
on Iran.

23
00:01:08,680 --> 00:01:13,480
They began just hours after Bill Clinton had testified to Congress about Epstein.

24
00:01:13,480 --> 00:01:18,840
The war was launched without a vote in Congress, within days a strange idea spread across both

25
00:01:18,840 --> 00:01:19,840
parties.

26
00:01:19,840 --> 00:01:24,440
Republican Congressman Thomas Massie, one of the men who forced the files out, said that

27
00:01:24,440 --> 00:01:28,440
bombing a country on the other side of the world would not make the Epstein files

28
00:01:28,440 --> 00:01:29,440
go away.

29
00:01:29,440 --> 00:01:33,280
Democrats like Alexandria Ocasio-Cortez said the same.

30
00:01:33,280 --> 00:01:37,680
People online started calling the war Operation Epstein Fury.

31
00:01:37,680 --> 00:01:41,960
One poll in March from a left-leaning group found more than half of voters thought the

32
00:01:41,960 --> 00:01:44,360
war was at least partly a distraction.

33
00:01:44,360 --> 00:01:49,560
The White House called that idea ridiculous and said only true morons could believe it.

34
00:01:49,560 --> 00:01:53,160
Whatever the reason, the war was real and so was the bill.

35
00:01:53,160 --> 00:01:57,000
Before that morning, a barrel of oil cost about $70.

36
00:01:57,000 --> 00:02:00,400
Iran answered with the one weapon that scares every economy on Earth.

37
00:02:00,400 --> 00:02:05,320
It shut the strait of Hormuz, the narrow strip of water between Iran and Oman that carries

38
00:02:05,320 --> 00:02:07,840
close to a fifth of the world's oil.

39
00:02:07,840 --> 00:02:10,240
Tanker traffic fell to almost nothing.

40
00:02:10,240 --> 00:02:14,920
The International Energy Agency called it the largest supply disruption in history.

41
00:02:14,920 --> 00:02:19,760
By the end of April, oil hit $126, the highest in four years.

42
00:02:19,760 --> 00:02:22,840
American gas jumped a full dollar in a single month.

43
00:02:22,880 --> 00:02:27,160
Later that year, a ceasefire came, then talks, then a deal on paper in June.

44
00:02:27,160 --> 00:02:31,080
It fell apart within weeks over who controls the strait.

45
00:02:31,080 --> 00:02:36,480
In July, the US Navy put its blockade of Iranian ports back in place and Iran kept hitting

46
00:02:36,480 --> 00:02:37,480
ships.

47
00:02:37,480 --> 00:02:41,080
October became the deadliest month for attacks on shipping in the whole war.

48
00:02:41,080 --> 00:02:43,880
Meanwhile, back home, the Epstein files never left.

49
00:02:43,880 --> 00:02:48,560
The Attorney General, Pam Bondi, was pushed out in April after criticism over how she

50
00:02:48,560 --> 00:02:49,800
handled them.

51
00:02:49,800 --> 00:02:54,520
The Commerce Secretary, Howard Lutnick, became the first sitting cabinet member to be questioned

52
00:02:54,520 --> 00:02:57,240
by Congress about his ties to Epstein.

53
00:02:57,240 --> 00:03:00,160
And every week, Americans paid more at the pump.

54
00:03:00,160 --> 00:03:06,240
One poll found that 63% of Americans blamed the president for high gas prices.

55
00:03:06,240 --> 00:03:08,160
Then came the third of November.

56
00:03:08,160 --> 00:03:10,440
The midterm elections were not close.

57
00:03:10,440 --> 00:03:11,920
Democrats took the House.

58
00:03:11,920 --> 00:03:17,200
Democrats took the Senate, flipping nine seats, the most for any party in nearly 70 years.

59
00:03:17,200 --> 00:03:22,320
They will hold 56 seats in the Senate and well over 250 in the House.

60
00:03:22,320 --> 00:03:25,560
It has been called the biggest blue wave since Watergate.

61
00:03:25,560 --> 00:03:27,560
And the war was a big part of why.

62
00:03:27,560 --> 00:03:33,120
A Reuters and Ipsos poll this month found 71% of Americans want Congress to pass a law

63
00:03:33,120 --> 00:03:36,520
ending it, including about half of Republicans.

64
00:03:36,520 --> 00:03:37,920
Watch what happened next.

65
00:03:37,920 --> 00:03:41,880
Within a week, the president said the war was militarily effectively over.

66
00:03:41,880 --> 00:03:43,800
And that new strikes were not needed.

67
00:03:43,800 --> 00:03:46,960
Oil dropped below $90 for the first time since August.

68
00:03:46,960 --> 00:03:48,840
Gas fell under four.

69
00:03:48,840 --> 00:03:50,880
So is that why oil is falling?

70
00:03:50,880 --> 00:03:51,880
Partly.

71
00:03:52,880 --> 00:03:56,080
But the bigger reason is something most people missed.

72
00:03:56,080 --> 00:03:57,760
The oil found another way out.

73
00:03:57,760 --> 00:04:01,280
Tankers started slipping through the southern side of the strait with their trackers switched

74
00:04:01,280 --> 00:04:02,280
off.

75
00:04:02,280 --> 00:04:04,400
Many of them guided by American forces.

76
00:04:04,400 --> 00:04:08,800
Gulf countries pushed more crude through pipelines that skip Hormuz completely.

77
00:04:08,800 --> 00:04:13,720
By October, Gulf crude exports were back above 80% of their pre-war level.

78
00:04:13,720 --> 00:04:17,880
And because the war made oil so expensive, the world burned less of it.

79
00:04:17,880 --> 00:04:23,480
On the 13th of November, the International Energy Agency said, supply is now bigger than

80
00:04:23,480 --> 00:04:26,840
demand for the first time since the war began.

81
00:04:26,840 --> 00:04:28,440
That is why the price is falling.

82
00:04:28,440 --> 00:04:32,040
Not because the war ended, because the world learned to live around it.

83
00:04:32,040 --> 00:04:33,600
And the war has not ended.

84
00:04:33,600 --> 00:04:37,880
Ship traffic through Hormuz is still about 65% below normal.

85
00:04:37,880 --> 00:04:39,680
Tankers are still being hit.

86
00:04:39,680 --> 00:04:43,280
A third American aircraft carrier just arrived in the region.

87
00:04:43,280 --> 00:04:48,360
CBS News reports Israel and the United States are considering a new assault on Iran.

88
00:04:48,360 --> 00:04:53,920
Iran has set seven conditions before it reopens the strait, starting with an end to the American

89
00:04:53,920 --> 00:04:54,920
blockade.

90
00:04:54,920 --> 00:04:59,040
And just days ago, the Senate rejected another attempt to limit the president's war

91
00:04:59,040 --> 00:05:00,040
powers.

92
00:05:00,040 --> 00:05:01,040
48 to 51.

93
00:05:01,040 --> 00:05:05,200
At the very same moment, the Epstein files came roaring back.

94
00:05:05,200 --> 00:05:10,840
On the 11th of November, Thomas Massie got the 218 signatures he needed to force a new

95
00:05:10,840 --> 00:05:16,560
House vote to release more Epstein files, because survivors and lawmakers say records

96
00:05:16,560 --> 00:05:18,800
are still being held back.

97
00:05:18,800 --> 00:05:23,160
On Thursday, Marjorie Taylor Greene, once one of the president's loudest allies, claimed

98
00:05:23,160 --> 00:05:25,640
that he personally blocked the files.

99
00:05:25,640 --> 00:05:29,800
That is her claim, and it has not been proven, but it tells you how much his own side has

100
00:05:29,800 --> 00:05:30,800
split.

101
00:05:30,800 --> 00:05:34,840
So now you have a president with two problems that both arrive in January.

102
00:05:34,840 --> 00:05:37,080
A war that most Americans want ended.

103
00:05:37,080 --> 00:05:39,680
And files that a new Congress wants opened.

104
00:05:39,680 --> 00:05:44,000
Because on the 3rd of January, the new Congress is sworn in, and Democrats get the power

105
00:05:44,000 --> 00:05:47,880
that matters most in Washington, subpoenas.

106
00:05:47,880 --> 00:05:51,200
They can force people to testify and hand over documents.

107
00:05:51,200 --> 00:05:53,720
They have already said what they want to investigate.

108
00:05:53,720 --> 00:05:57,720
The decision to go to war with Iran without asking Congress.

109
00:05:57,720 --> 00:05:59,720
The handling of the Epstein files.

110
00:05:59,720 --> 00:06:01,560
The president's business interests.

111
00:06:01,560 --> 00:06:06,200
The top Democrat on the House Foreign Affairs Committee says that in January, he will bring

112
00:06:06,200 --> 00:06:10,600
a war powers resolution and support cutting off money for the war.

113
00:06:10,600 --> 00:06:15,800
And with control of both chambers, Democrats can write into must-pass spending bills that

114
00:06:15,800 --> 00:06:18,120
no money may be used to fight Iran.

115
00:06:18,120 --> 00:06:19,320
There are limits.

116
00:06:19,320 --> 00:06:23,560
Trump still has a veto, and Democrats do not have enough votes to override it on their

117
00:06:23,560 --> 00:06:24,560
own.

118
00:06:24,560 --> 00:06:29,400
But they control the money, and money is what keeps three aircraft carriers at sea.

119
00:06:29,400 --> 00:06:32,760
That is why the weeks before January matter so much.

120
00:06:32,760 --> 00:06:37,040
Some analysts say that if there is going to be a big new military move, it is likely

121
00:06:37,040 --> 00:06:39,400
to come before the new Congress takes over.

122
00:06:39,400 --> 00:06:43,440
And Trump told Israeli television this week that he is not rushing,

123
00:06:43,440 --> 00:06:47,200
and that we will see what happens after the new year starts.

124
00:06:47,200 --> 00:06:49,360
Before that there are two dates to watch.

125
00:06:49,360 --> 00:06:55,440
On the 29th of November, the OPEC plus oil producers decide how much oil to pump next

126
00:06:55,440 --> 00:06:56,440
year.

127
00:06:56,440 --> 00:07:00,600
And on the 11th of December, the government runs out of money, and Democrats have talked

128
00:07:00,600 --> 00:07:04,120
about using that deadline to pressure the president to end the war.

129
00:07:04,120 --> 00:07:06,400
So what happens to oil in January?

130
00:07:06,400 --> 00:07:08,160
It comes down to three roads.

131
00:07:08,160 --> 00:07:12,720
If there is a deal, the blockade lifts and the strait reopens, even with a toll, and

132
00:07:12,720 --> 00:07:18,040
the calmer forecasts point toward the 70s, close to where oil was before the war began.

133
00:07:18,040 --> 00:07:23,280
If nothing changes, a frozen war where ships slip through in the dark, oil likely stays

134
00:07:23,280 --> 00:07:25,200
stuck around where it is now.

135
00:07:25,200 --> 00:07:29,760
And if the strikes start again before the new Congress arrives, analysts have warned

136
00:07:29,840 --> 00:07:32,800
that crude could jump toward 150.

137
00:07:32,800 --> 00:07:34,800
Even the big banks cannot agree.

138
00:07:34,800 --> 00:07:40,640
For the first three months of next year, BNP Paribas expects about $78 a barrel.

139
00:07:40,640 --> 00:07:42,720
Morgan Stanley says 100.

140
00:07:42,720 --> 00:07:47,160
That $22 gap is the price of not knowing what happens in Washington.

141
00:07:47,160 --> 00:07:51,160
But there is one price that will not come down on any of those roads.

142
00:07:51,160 --> 00:07:52,160
Diesel.

143
00:07:52,160 --> 00:07:54,520
Diesel moves the trucks that carry your groceries.

144
00:07:54,520 --> 00:07:58,400
The war hit refineries and fuel shipments even harder than crude.

145
00:07:58,400 --> 00:08:03,200
And the US government now expects diesel to average about $5 a gallon next year.

146
00:08:03,200 --> 00:08:07,560
This Thanksgiving is already on track to be the most expensive ever at the pump.

147
00:08:07,560 --> 00:08:09,760
So are oil prices finally dropping?

148
00:08:09,760 --> 00:08:10,760
Yes.

149
00:08:10,760 --> 00:08:12,400
But not because the war is over.

150
00:08:12,400 --> 00:08:15,200
They are dropping because the world found a way around it.

151
00:08:15,200 --> 00:08:19,560
And because voters just took the steering wheel away from one side of Washington.

152
00:08:19,560 --> 00:08:23,320
Now a war that may have been launched in the shadow of the Epstein files could be ended

153
00:08:23,320 --> 00:08:27,600
or escalated in the shadow of the new Congress coming to open them.

154
00:08:27,600 --> 00:08:33,320
The 29th of November, the 11th of December, the 3rd of January, those three dates.

155
00:08:33,320 --> 00:08:36,280
And yes, it seems like war can finally stop.

156
00:08:36,280 --> 00:08:36,760
Peace!
